-- mirror_cloud.fleet -- two machines on one wire, one of which keeps the other's world's directory (MIR-1, fleet v0.5).
--
-- The loss of one machine must not be the loss of what it held, and STZ-OS-RULING-19 gives the fleet the means: a
-- MIRROR, a declared copy of a world's directory on another member, over a link the fleet names, verified by the
-- fleet's keys. Each machine says only its own end -- the source whom it gives to (a key), the keeper whom it takes
-- from (an address, a port and a key) -- and each is faultless alone while the pair does not meet. The court holds
-- the pair to each other before anything boots: the keeper asks the address and port the source gives on, takes the
-- word of the source's enrolled key, is the device the source gives to, and has a way there; and no machine gives
-- or takes a copy this file never named (FR74-FR93).
--
-- TERRITORY says where each member physically stands. Here they stand apart on purpose -- the copy is worth having
-- because it is not in the room the original is in -- and no RESIDENCY holds them together. A fleet whose data must
-- stay in one place says so with a RESIDENCY, and a keeper standing anywhere else is refused by the rule that already
-- holds every member that keeps a disk (FR91): the mirror needed no rule of its own for it.
--
-- KEY below is a placeholder for each, as it is in machines/time_cloud.fleet: a device makes its own key on its first
-- boot and a file in a repository cannot know it. experiment/os12_mirror.sh boots both, reads the public halves they
-- publish and writes them in COPIES of this file and of the two machine files, which is what enrolment is.

DEFINE FLEET boutique AS (
  LINK lan
) RATIONALE "A shop's till machine and the machine in the warehouse that keeps a copy of its ledger"

DEFINE MEMBER depot AS (
  DECLARATION "mirror_source.machine",
  KEY "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
  HARDWARE "52:54:00:12:37:01",
  TERRITORY shop
) RATIONALE "The machine whose world keeps the ledger, standing in the shop, enrolled so that the listing it signs can be checked by anyone holding this file"

DEFINE MEMBER annex AS (
  DECLARATION "mirror_keeper.machine",
  KEY "abababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababab",
  HARDWARE "52:54:00:12:37:02",
  TERRITORY warehouse
) RATIONALE "The machine that keeps the copy, standing in the warehouse, enrolled so that the source can be shown to give the copy to it and to nobody else"

DEFINE MIRROR ledger_copy AS (
  FROM depot,
  TO annex
) RATIONALE "The shop's ledger is kept in the warehouse too: the shop burning down must not take the records with it"
